  },
  {
   "measure": "Percentage of Participants Who Experience At Least One Serious Adverse Event (SAE)",
   "description": "An AE was any untoward medical occurrence in a participant, temporally associated with the use of study treatment, whether or not considered related to the study treatment. An SAE was defined as any untoward medical occurrence that, at any dose: resulted in death, was life-threatening, required inpatient hospitalization or prolongation of existing hospitalization, resulted in persistent or significant disability/incapacity, was a congenital anomaly/birth defect, or was another important medical event. The number of participants with an SAE was reported.",
