 "primaryOutcomes": [
  {
   "measure": "Area Under the Curve (AUC) 0-30min Standardized by Time of Change From Pre-dose in Forced Expiratory Volume in One Second (FEV1) in the Morning of Day 1",
   "description": "FEV1 is a measure of lung function and is defined as the maximal amount of air that can be forcefully exhaled in one second. FEV1 was measured using spirometry, conducted at baseline and all clinical visits. An increase in FEV1 reflects improved airway patency, while a decrease suggests worsening obstruction. Higher FEV1 values indicate better lung function. Adjusted means were reported. Assessment were implemented at pre-dose, and 5, 15 and 30 minutes post inhalation",
   "timeFrame": "on Day 1 (V2)"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Transition Dyspnoea Index (TDI) Score at Day 84",
   "description": "TDI has three domains as follows:\n\n1. Functional impairment, which determines the impact of breathlessness on the ability to carry out activities;\n2. Magnitude of task, which determines the type of task that causes breathlessness;\n3. Magnitude of effort, which establishes the level of effort that results in breathlessness\n\nThe TDI score ranges from -3 (major deterioration) to +3 (major improvement) for each domain. The sum of all domains yields the TDI focal score of -9 (major deterioration) to +9 (major improvement).\n\nAdjusted means were reported.",
   "timeFrame": "Day 84 (V5)"
