   "description": "Percentage of participants achieving ≥75% reduction from baseline in PASI-75 at Week 12 without use of background antipsoriasis therapy were responders. The PASI measures psoriasis severity based on lesion characteristics and body surface area (BSA) affected. Erythema, thickness, and scaling are each scored from 0 (none) to 4 (very severe) across four regions: head, trunk, upper limbs, and lower limbs. Area involvement in each region is graded from 0 (none) to 6 (90-100%). The sum of severity scores for erythema, thickness, and scaling is multiplied by the degree of involvement for each anatomic region and a region-specific BSA weight (0.1, 0.3, 0.2, 0.4). Regional scores are summed to give a total PASI score ranging from 0 to 72, with higher values indicating greater severity.",
