   "description": "A participant is counted if a first stroke (ischemic or hemorrhagic) occurred after randomization during the on-treatment period. Time-to-event analysis was performed using a stratified Cox proportional hazards model to compare treatment groups over the follow-up period.",
   "timeFrame": "Up to 32 months"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Number of Participants Who Had Composite of Cardiovascular Death, Myocardial Infarction, or Stroke",
   "description": "A participant is counted if a first occurrence of cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction, or stroke occurred after randomization. Time-to-event analysis was performed using a stratified Cox proportional hazards model to compare treatment groups over the follow-up period.",
   "timeFrame": "Up to 32 months"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Number of Participants Who Had Composite of All-cause Mortality, Myocardial Infarction, or Stroke",
   "description": "A participant is counted if a first occurrence of all-cause mortality, myocardial infarction, or stroke occurred after randomization. Time-to-event analysis was performed using a stratified Cox proportional hazards model to compare treatment groups over the follow-up period.",
   "timeFrame": "Up to 32 months"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Number of Participants Who Had Disabling Stroke (mRS ≥3 at 90 Days)",
   "description": "A participant is counted if a first disabling stroke occurred after randomization. Disabling stroke is defined as a stroke of any type associated with a modified Rankin Scale (mRS) score ≥3 at 90 days after the recurrent stroke, or an increase of ≥1 point if the last available mRS before the recurrent stroke was ≥3. Fatal strokes are included. Time-to-event analysis was performed using a stratified Cox proportional hazards model to compare treatment groups over the follow-up period.",
   "timeFrame": "Up to 32 months"
