   "measure": "Annualized Rate of Moderate and Severe COPD Exacerbations Over the 52-Week Treatment Period",
   "description": "A moderate COPD exacerbation was defined as new or increased COPD symptoms (e.g., dyspnea, sputum volume, and sputum purulence) that lead to treatment (duration ≥ 3 days) with systemic corticosteroids (oral, intravenous \\[IV\\], or intramuscular \\[IM\\]) at a dose of \\> 10 milligrams per day (mg/day) prednisolone equivalent and/or antibiotics. A severe COPD exacerbation was defined as new or increased COPD symptoms that lead to hospitalization (duration \\> 24 hours) or death. The unadjusted annual exacerbation rate (AER) was estimated as the total number of moderate and severe COPD exacerbations over the treatment period divided by the total patient-years at risk. The time at risk (in years) was the number of days from the date of first administration of study drug to the date of study completion or discontinuation in the 52-week treatment period, divided by 365.25 days. The adjusted AER was estimated using a negative binomial regression model. Adjusted rate values have been reported.",
