   "description": "A moderate COPD exacerbation was defined as new or increased COPD symptoms (e.g., dyspnea, sputum volume, and sputum purulence) that lead to treatment (duration ≥ 3 days) with systemic corticosteroids (oral, IV, or IM) at a dose of \\>10 mg/day prednisolone equivalent and/or antibiotics. A severe COPD exacerbation was defined as new or increased COPD symptoms that led to hospitalization (duration \\> 24 hours) or death. Unadjusted AER was estimated as the total number of moderate and severe COPD exacerbations over the treatment period divided by the total patient-years at risk. The time at risk (in years) was the number of days from the date of first administration of study drug to the date of study completion or discontinuation in the 52-week treatment period, divided by 365.25 days. The adjusted AER was estimated using a negative binomial regression model. Adjusted rate values are reported. Number analyzed is the number of participants with data available for analysis.",
   "timeFrame": "Baseline to Week 52"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Time to First Moderate or Severe COPD Exacerbation During the 52-Week Treatment Period",
   "description": "Time to first moderate or severe COPD exacerbation was defined as the time from the first administration of study drug to the first incidence of moderate or severe COPD exacerbation event during the 52-week treatment period. A moderate COPD exacerbation is defined as new or increased COPD symptoms (e.g., dyspnea, sputum volume, and sputum purulence) that lead to treatment (duration ≥ 3 days) with systemic corticosteroids (oral, IV, or IM) at a dose of \\> 10 mg/day prednisolone equivalent and/or antibiotics. A severe COPD exacerbation is defined as new or increased COPD symptoms that lead to hospitalization (duration \\> 24 hours) or lead to death. Kaplan-Meier (K-M) method was used to estimate the median time.",
   "timeFrame": "Baseline up to Week 52"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Absolute Change From Baseline in Health-related Quality-of-life (HRQoL) at Week 52, as Assessed Through the St. George's Respiratory Questionnaire-COPD (SGRQ-C) Total Score",
   "description": "SGRQ-C is a disease-specific, self-administered instrument designed to assess the impact of COPD on participants' health status and well-being based on their perception of COPD-related experiences. The questionnaire consists of 40 items across three sub-domains: symptoms (respiratory symptoms and severity- 7 items), activity (activities causing or limited by breathlessness-13 items) and impacts (social functioning and psychological disturbances due to airway disease- 20 items). Each response is assigned a unique empirically derived weight. Total score is calculated by summing the weights to all the positive responses across each domain, with scores ranging from 0 (no impairment) to 100 (maximum impairment), with lower scores indicating better HRQoL. This analysis used a Mixed Model for Repeated Measurements (MMRM) model. Adjusted mean of change from baseline (CFB) is reported here.",
   "timeFrame": "At Week 52"
  },
