   "measure": "Percentage of Participants With Improvement in HRQoL at Week 52, as Assessed Through SGRQ-C Total Score",
   "description": "Percentage of participants with SGRQ-C improvement was defined as the percentage of participants with an absolute decrease from baseline of ≥4 points in SGRQ-C total score. SGRQ-C is a disease-specific, self-administered instrument designed to assess the impact of COPD on participants' health status and well-being based on their perception of COPD-related experiences. The questionnaire consists of 40 items across three sub-domains: symptoms (respiratory symptoms and severity- 7 items), activity (activities causing or limited by breathlessness-13 items) and impacts (social functioning and psychological disturbances due to airway disease- 20 items). Each response is assigned a unique empirically derived weight. Total score is calculated by summing the weights to all the positive responses across each domain, with scores ranging from 0 (no impairment) to 100 (maximum impairment), with lower scores indicating better HRQoL.",
   "timeFrame": "At Week 52"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Absolute Change From Baseline in Post-bronchodilator Forced Expiratory Volume in 1 Second (FEV1) (Liters) at Week 52",
   "description": "Post-bronchodilator FEV1 was defined as the FEV1 value measured with spirometry 20-30 minutes after bronchodilator use. Maximal bronchodilation was achieved via administration of either albuterol (90 micrograms \\[µg\\] metered dose) or salbutamol (100 µg metered dose), with or without a spacer device, up to a maximum of 4 inhalations. This analysis used a MMRM model. Adjusted mean of CFB is reported here.",
   "timeFrame": "At Week 52"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Absolute Change From Baseline in Evaluating Respiratory Symptoms in COPD (E-RS:COPD) Total Score at Week 52",
   "description": "EXAcerbations of Chronic Pulmonary Disease Tool (EXACT) is a 14-item participant-reported instrument used to assess frequency, severity, \\& duration of COPD exacerbations using a daily electronic diary (eDiary). It includes four domains: breathlessness (5 items), cough and sputum (3 items), chest symptoms (3 items), and additional attributes (tired or weak, sleep disturbance, and scared or worried; 3 items). The E-RS:COPD is an 11-item subset of the EXACT designed to assess the severity of cardinal respiratory symptoms of COPD, including breathlessness, cough, sputum, chest congestion, and chest tightness. It consists of three subscales: RS-Breathlessness, RS-Cough \\& Sputum, and RS-Chest Symptoms. Items are scored on 5- or 6-point Likert scales, and the total score is calculated by summing the item scores, ranging from 0 (no impact) to 40 (high impact), with higher scores indicating greater symptom severity. This analysis used a MMRM model. Adjusted mean of CFB has been reported here.",
