   "measure": "Number of Participants With TEAEs and Treatment-Related TEAEs by Severity: Part A",
   "description": "An AE was defined as any untoward medical occurrence in participant administered an investigational product and which does not necessarily have causal relationship with treatment. A TEAE was defined as any AE which on or after exposure to study treatment up to 28 days following the last dose. Treatment related TEAEs were TEAEs that were related to study drug and relatedness was judged by investigator. Severity: mild: asymptomatic/ mild symptoms, clinical/ diagnostic observations only, intervention not indicated; moderate: minimal, local/ non-invasive intervention indicated, limiting age-appropriate instrumental activities of daily living and severe: medically significant but not immediately life-threatening, hospitalization/ prolongation of hospitalization indicated, disabling, limiting self-care activities of daily living/ life-threatening consequences, urgent intervention indicated/ death related to an AE.",
   "timeFrame": "Up to Week 37"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Number of Participants With Abnormal Clinically Significant Physical Examination: Part A",
   "description": "The physical examination included examination of the following body systems (at minimum): head and neck (including complete thyroid exam), cardiovascular, respiratory, gastrointestinal, brief neurological, and general appearance. Clinical significance will be judged by investigator.",
   "timeFrame": "From Day 1 of dosing up to post treatment follow up for Part A"
  },
