  {
   "measure": "Time to Confirmed Deterioration (TTCD) in Physical Functioning, Role Functioning & Global Health Status/Quality of Life (GHS/QoL), Assessed by European Organisation for Research & Treatment of Cancer Quality of Life Questionnaire-Core 30 (EORTC QLQ-C30)",
   "description": "TTCD of physical functioning (PF), role functioning (RF) \\& health-related quality of life (HRQoL) was defined as time from randomization to first documented confirmed deterioration. Confirmed deterioration=participant's first ≥10-point score decrease from baseline on EORTC QLQ C30 PF, RF or GHS/QoL scale that must be held for ≤2 consecutive time points or followed by death due to cancer progression within 8 weeks from last patient-reported outcomes (PRO) assessment. EORTC QLQ-C30 has 30 questions assessing 5 aspects of participant functioning (physical, emotional, role, cognitive \\& social), 3 symptom scales (fatigue, nausea \\& vomiting \\& pain), GHS/QoL \\& 6 single items (dyspnea, insomnia, appetite loss, constipation, diarrhea \\& financial difficulties). Functioning items are scored on a 4-point scale (1=Not at All to 4=Very Much) \\& GHS/QoL on a 7-point scale (1=very poor to 7=excellent). Scores are linearly transformed on a scale of 0 to 100. High score=better functioning/better QoL.",
