   "timeFrame": "Baseline (Day 1) and Week 26"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Change From Baseline to Week 26 in Patient Health Questionnaire, 9-Item (PHQ-9) Total Score",
   "description": "Change from baseline to Week 26 in PHQ-9 total score was reported. The PHQ-9 is a 9-item, participant reported outcome measure to assess depressive symptoms. The scale scores each of the 9 symptom domains of the diagnostic and statistical manual of mental disorders-5th edition (DSM-5) major depressive disorder (MDD) criteria. Each item was rated on a 4 point scale (0=not at all, 1=several days, 2=more than half the days, and 3=nearly every day). The participant's item responses are summed to provide a total score (range of 0 to 27), with higher scores indicating greater severity of depressive symptoms. Negative changes in PHQ-9 total score indicated improvement.",
