   "description": "The TEAE of special interest in this study included documented events of orthostatic hypotension (OHT) with supine and standing blood pressure measurements, where OHT is defined as a drop in blood pressure from supine to standing position:\n\n* of ≥20 mmHg in systolic blood pressure (SBP), and/or\n* of ≥10 mmHg in diastolic blood pressure (DBP).",
