   "description": "The ADAS-Cog was a rater administered instrument that was designed to assess the severity of dysfunction in cognition characteristic of persons with Alzheimer's Disease (AD). The ADAS-Cog13 item scale includes all items from the original ADAS-Cog11 (consisting of 11 tasks measuring the disturbances of memory, language, praxis, attention, and other cognitive abilities, often referred to as the core symptoms of AD) in addition of number cancellation task and a delayed free recall task, for a total of 85 points (0 to 85), with higher scores indicating worse cognitive performance.",
   "timeFrame": "Baseline (Day 1), Week 104"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Double-blind (DB) Treatment Period: Change From Baseline in Alzheimer's Disease Cooperative Study Activities of Daily Living for Mild Cognitive Impairment (ADCS-ADL-MCI) Total Score at Week 104",
   "description": "The ADCS-ADL-MCI was a functional measure based on information provided by the study partner that describes the performance of participants in several activities of daily living. The ADCS-ADL-MCI scale consists of 17 instrumental items (example; shopping, preparing meals, using household appliances, etc) and 1 basic item (getting dressed). The ADCS-ADL-MCI scale version used in this study comprises 24 items of which 18 items are used for the standard analysis. The total score ranges from 0 to 53 with higher scores indicating less impairment. A positive change from baseline indicates healthy functioning while a negative change from baseline indicates a decline in independent functioning.",
   "timeFrame": "Baseline (Day 1), Week 104"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Double-blind (DB) Treatment Period: Change From Baseline in Repeatable Battery for the Assessment of Neuropsychological Status (RBANS) Total Scale Index Score at Week 88",
   "description": "The RBANS was a battery developed for cognitive assessment, detection, and characterization of dementia. RBANS includes 12 subtests that are divided into 5 RBANS indices: Immediate memory (list learning and story memory), visuospatial/constructional (figure copy and line orientation), language (picture naming and semantic fluency), attention (digit span and coding) and delayed memory (list recall, list recognition, story recall, and figure recall). Index scores are expressed as an age-adjusted standard score with a normal mean of 100 and an standard deviation (SD) of 15. Sum of index scores was the sum of the 5 index scores, and the Sum of Index Scores was converted to an RBANS total scale index score via a mapping table. The RBANS total scale Index score was a norm-based t-score, based on a distribution with a mean of 100 and an SD of 15. Scores range from 40 to 160. Higher scores indicated better performance.",
   "timeFrame": "Baseline (Day 1), Week 88"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Double-blind (DB) Treatment Period: Change From Baseline in Each of the 5 Individuals RBANS Indices at Week 88",
