   "timeFrame": "Baseline (Day 1), Week 88"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Double-blind (DB) Treatment Period: Change From Baseline in Each of the 12 Subtests Comprising the RBANS at Week 88",
   "description": "The RBANS was a battery developed for cognitive assessment, detection, and characterization of dementia. RBANS includes 12 subtests that are divided into 5 RBANS indices: Immediate memory (list learning \\[0-40\\] and story memory \\[0-24\\]), visuospatial/constructional (figure copy \\[0-20\\] and line orientation \\[0-20\\]), language (picture naming \\[0-10\\] and semantic fluency \\[0-40\\]), attention (digit span \\[0-16\\] and coding \\[0-89\\]) and delayed memory (list recall \\[0-10\\], list recognition \\[0-20\\], story recall \\[0-12\\], and figure recall \\[0-20\\]). Index scores are expressed as an age-adjusted standard score with a normal mean of 100 and an SD of 15. Sum of index scores was the sum of the 5 index scores, and the Sum of Index Scores was converted to an RBANS total scale index score via a mapping table. Scores range from 40 to 160. Higher scores indicated better performance.",
