  "description": "The iADRS-MCI was a composite measure of cognition and function. It was originally developed as a combination of the Alzheimer's Disease Assessment Scale-Cognitive (ADAS-Cog) 14-item cognition subscale and the instrumental activities of daily living (ADL) items from the Alzheimer's Disease Cooperative Study Activities of Daily Living (ADCS-ADL) scale. It was calculated as a linear combination of total scores of the 2 individual components. The iADRS-MCI total score was derived as a combination of the ADAS-Cog13 total score (ranging from 0 to 85, with higher scores indicating worse cognitive performance) and the ADCS-ADL-MCI total score (ranging from 0 to 53, with lower scores indicating worse daily function). Therefore, the iADRS-MCI total score was calculated as \\[-1(ADAS-Cog13 score)+85\\] + ADCS-ADL-MCI score, ranging from 0 to 138, with lower scores indicating worse performance.",
