   "timeFrame": "Baseline to Week 52 and 78"
  },
  {
   "measure": "The Change in Cognitive Function Assessed by Clinical Dementia Rating Scale Sum of Boxes (CDR-sb) From Baseline to Weeks 28, 52, and 78",
   "description": "The CDR is a global rating scale for staging patients diagnosed with dementia. CDR is calculated on the basis of testing six different cognitive and behavioral domains such as memory, orientation, judgment and problem solving, community affairs, home and hobbies performance, and personal care. The CDR is based on a scale of 0-3: no dementia (CDR = 0), questionable dementia (CDR = 0.5), mild cognitive impairment (CDR = 1), moderate cognitive impairment (CDR = 2), and severe cognitive impairment (CDR = 3). The sum of these 6 areas, the CDR-sb score, range from 0 (perfect performance) to 18 (worse).",
   "timeFrame": "Baseline to Week 28, 52 and 78"
  },
  {
   "measure": "The Change in Cognitive Function Assessed by Cognitive Functional Composite (CFC) From Baseline to Weeks 28, 52, and 78",
   "description": "The CFC is expected to detect clinically relevant changes in early dementia stages of AD, and comprises cognitive and functional components.\n\nThe cognitive composite is computed as a weighted z-score of all seven cognitive subtests: Alzheimer's Disease Assessment Scale-Cognitive Subscale \\[ADAS-Cog; 3 subscores (Orientation, Word Recall, Word Recognition), range 0-30\\], Digit Span Backward Task (range 0-12), Controlled Oral Word Association Test (1 point for each correct non-repeated word), Category Fluency Test (1 point for each correct unique animal), Digit Symbol Substitution Test (1 point for each correct substituted symbol).\n\nThe functional component consists of the Amsterdam Instrumental Activity of Daily Living Questionnaire-short version (A-IADL-Q-SV) and the scoring is based on item response theory.\n\nThe overall CFC score is computed as an equally weighted z-score of the overall cognitive composite and IADL latent trait z-score.\n\n(Continued to \"Analysis Population Description\")",
