   "description": "An EEG was derived at Baseline and at Weeks 52 and 78 to measure global relative power in the theta band (4 to 8 Hz). Relative theta power has been regarded as the most sensitive marker of EEG oscillatory activity in early AD. In addition, relative power in the alpha band (8 to 13 Hz) and alpha/theta ratio were evaluated. Alpha/theta ratio of the EEG has been reported as a new marker for AD.",
   "timeFrame": "Baseline to Week 52 and 78"
  },
  {
   "measure": "Population Pharmacokinetic (PK) Analysis of T-817MA With Assessment of Maximum Plasma Concentration at Steady State (Css-max)",
   "description": "Blood samples for population PK (PPK) analysis were collected at Weeks 16, 28, 40, and 65 in MCI due to AD or mild AD Phase 2 study (EU201) with a single blood draw at each of these visits.\n\nThe PPK analysis was performed on the basis of data collected in the eight Phase 1 studies, two AD Phase 2 studies (JP201 and US202), and EU201 Study (a total of 6753 data from 702 individuals).\n\nPopulation parameters (Ka, LF1, CL/F, Q/F, Vc/F, Vp/F) were calculated considering intra- and inter-individual variability and covariates. Individual post-hoc PK parameters were estimated using the final population parameters and the individual patient data. T-817 plasma concentration-time profiles were predicted by the individual post-hoc PK parameters. Individual Cmax values of T-817 at steady state (Week 78) were derived and used as Css-max, and then summarized as statistics.\n\nAbbreviations of PK parameters are explained in the Analysis Population Description.",
   "timeFrame": "Prior to dosing on the day of the Weeks 28 and 65 clinic visit, and 1 to 6 hours after the time that the last study drug was taken on the scheduled visit day at Weeks 16 and 40."
  },
  {
   "measure": "PPK Analysis of T-817MA With Assessment of Minimum Plasma Concentration at Steady State (Css-min)",
   "description": "Blood samples for population PK (PPK) analysis were collected at Weeks 16, 28, 40, and 65 in MCI due to AD or mild AD Phase 2 study (EU201) with a single blood draw at each of these visits.\n\nThe PPK analysis was performed on the basis of data collected in the eight Phase 1 studies, two AD Phase 2 studies (JP201 and US202), and EU201 Study (a total of 6753 data from 702 individuals).\n\nPopulation parameters (Ka, LF1, CL/F, Q/F, Vc/F, Vp/F) were calculated considering intra- and inter-individual variability and covariates. Individual post-hoc PK parameters were estimated using the final population parameters and the individual patient data. T-817 plasma concentration-time profiles were predicted by the individual post-hoc PK parameters. Individual Cmin values of T-817 at steady state (Week 78) were derived and used as Css-min, and then summarized as statistics.",
   "timeFrame": "Prior to dosing on the day of the Weeks 28 and 65 clinic visit, and 1 to 6 hours after the time that the last study drug was taken on the scheduled visit day at Weeks 16 and 40."
  },
  {
   "measure": "PPK Analysis of T-817MA With Assessment of Area Under the Plasma Concentration-time Curve During a Dosage Interval at Steady State (AUCss-tau)",
   "description": "Blood samples for PPK analysis were collected at Weeks 16, 28, 40, and 65 in MCI due to AD or mild AD Phase 2 study (EU201) with a single blood draw at each of these visits.\n\nThe PPK analysis was performed on the basis of data collected in the eight Phase 1 studies, two AD Phase 2 studies (JP201 and US202), and EU201 Study (a total of 6753 data from 702 individuals).\n\nPopulation parameters (Ka, LF1, CL/F, Q/F, Vc/F, Vp/F) were calculated considering intra- and inter-individual variability and covariates. Individual post-hoc PK parameters were estimated using the final population parameters and the individual patient data. T-817 plasma concentration-time profiles were predicted by the individual post-hoc PK parameters. Individual AUC values of T-817 during a dosage interval at steady state (Week 78) were derived and used as AUCss-tau, and then summarized as statistics.",
   "timeFrame": "Prior to dosing on the day of the Weeks 28 and 65 clinic visit, and 1 to 6 hours after the time that the last study drug was taken on the scheduled visit day at Weeks 16 and 40."
  },
  {
   "measure": "The Ratio of T-817 Levels in CSF to Plasma (CSF/Plasma)",
   "description": "CSF/plasma Ratio = (Observed CSF concentration of T-817)/(Predicted plasma concentration of T-817).\n\nAlthough the study protocol stated that CSF samples would be collected at Weeks 52 and 78, the actual collections occurred at at least either of Week 52 or Week 78. When the CSF analytical sample at Week 78 was not obtained or the sampling date for Week 78 was not the last T-817 administration date before sampling, the sample at Week 52 or at the point of discontinuation was analyzed. When these samples were not collected closer to the last administration time than the sample at Week 78, the sample at Week 78 was analyzed. CSF concentrations at both of Week 52 and 78 were analyzed for one patient, resulting in a total of 78 data points from 77 individuals, including 28 at Week 52 and 50 at Week 78. Plasma concentrations were predicted by PPK analysis. Individual CSF/plasma ratios at either of Week 52 or/and 78 were derived, pooled and then summarized as statistics.",
   "timeFrame": "Between 11:00 AM and 2:00 PM on Week 52 and 78."
  }
 ],
 "eligibility": {
  "criteria": "Key Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Female of non-childbearing potential or male, ages 50 to 80 years (inclusive)\n* MCI due to AD or mild AD per National Institute on Aging-Alzheimer's Association (NIA-AA) diagnostic criteria (Jack et al., 2018), with Mini Mental Status Examination (MMSE) 24 to 30 (inclusive)\n* CSF results at Screening consistent with the presence of amyloid ß (Aß) and p-tau181 abnormality (≤1000 pg/ml for Aß, ≥19 pg/ml for p-tau181).\n* Taking stable dose of acetylcholinesterase (AChE) Inhibitor (donepezil, galantamine or rivastigmine) at least for 3 months prior to randomization, or not taking any AChE Inhibitors.\n\nKey Exclusion Criteria:\n\n* MRI of the brain within the previous 2 years that showed pathology that would be inconsistent with a diagnosis of AD\n* Taking memantine\n* Any contraindications to lumbar puncture\n* Any contraindications to MRI",
