   "measure": "Period 1: Percentage of Participants Achieving ≥75% Reduction From Baseline in Psoriasis Area and Severity Index (PASI-75) at Week 16",
   "description": "Participants achieving a ≥75% reduction from baseline in Psoriasis Area and Severity Index (PASI) score (PASI 75) at Week 16 were considered responders. The PASI measures psoriasis severity based on lesion characteristics and body surface area (BSA) affected. Erythema, thickness, and scaling are each scored from 0 (none) to 4 (very severe) across four regions: head, trunk, upper limbs, and lower limbs. Area involvement in each region is graded from 0 (none) to 6 (90-100%). The sum of severity scores for erythema, thickness, and scaling is multiplied by the degree of involvement for each anatomic region and a region-specific BSA weight (0.1, 0.3, 0.2, 0.4). Regional scores are summed to give a total PASI score ranging from 0 to 72, with higher values indicating greater severity.\n\nAs pre-specified in the statistical analysis plan this analysis was planned to compare each VTX958 dose with Placebo.",
