   "description": "Percentage of participants with disease response according to STAR composite score at Week 24 was reported. STAR was a composite endpoint assessing multiple clinically relevant disease features. A STAR response was defined as a composite score of \\>=5 points in the 5 STAR domains, with weighting in parentheses: (i) decrease of \\>=3 in clinESSDAI score (3), (ii) decrease of \\>=1 point or \\>=15% from baseline in ESSPRI score (3), (iii) abnormal Schirmer's test at baseline and increase of \\>=5 millimeter (mm)/normal Schirmer's test at baseline and no change to abnormal/abnormal ocular staining score at baseline and a decrease of \\>=2 points/normal ocular staining score at baseline and no change to abnormal (1), (iv) increase of \\>=25% in unstimulated whole saliva/any increase if score is 0 at baseline (1), (v) decrease of \\>=25% in rheumatoid factor/decrease of \\>=10% in immunoglobulin G (IgG) (1). Overall score was sum of all domain weight, which range from 0 to 9 (higher score = worse outcome).",
