   "measure": "Change From Baseline in Weekly Urticaria Activity Score at Week 4",
   "description": "The UAS7 score is a composite score containing both the hive severity score (HSS, ranging from 0 = None to 3 = more than 50 hives) and the itch severity score (ISS, ranging from 0 = None to 3 = intense). The daily UAS scores ranged from 0 to 6 points per day. Daily UAS scores were summed over a 7-day period to create the UAS7, ranging from 0 to 42, and are composed of the HSS7 and ISS7 components. A higher score indicates worse disease. Baseline is defined as the sum of the 7 measurements obtained within the 7 days prior to randomization.",
