   "measure": "Former Smoker Cohort: Annualized Rate of Adjudicated Moderate or Severe Acute Exacerbation of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (AECOPD) Events Over the 52-Week Placebo-Controlled Treatment Period",
   "description": "Exacerbations were recorded by Investigator. Moderate exacerbations were defined as acute worsening of respiratory symptoms that required either systemic corticosteroids (such as intramuscular \\[IM\\], intravenous \\[IV\\], or oral) and/or antibiotics. Severe exacerbations were defined as AECOPD that required hospitalization, observation for \\>24 hours in an emergency department/urgent care facility, or resulted in death. For both moderate and severe events to be counted as 2 separate events, they must be separated by at least 14 days between any course of systemic steroids/antibiotics or 14 days between discharge and new admission in case of hospitalization (severe events only). Annualized rate was total number of moderate or severe exacerbation events divided by total observation duration and was estimated based on negative binomial regression. Events were adjudicated by third party.",
