   "description": "PGIC is a single item, self-administered questionnaire to assess the patient's global impression of change. The PGIC scale uses a 7-point rating format where participants select the response that best describes how their condition has changed: 1 = Very much improved, 2 = Much improved; 3 = Minimally improved; 4 = No change; 5 = Minimally worse; 6 = Much worse; 7 = Very much worse. LS mean and SE were calculated using ANCOVA model, which included treatment as fixed effect.",
